<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand von Steinbeis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1807–1893</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand von Steinbeis was a German economic official who directed industrial policy in the Kingdom of Württemberg from 1848 to 1880. At the central office for trade and industry he promoted vocational and technical schools, trade exhibitions, sample collections and the transfer of foreign techniques, helping turn Württemberg from a poor agrarian state into an industrial region. The Steinbeis Foundation is named after him.</p></div>
